<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>My Paper Keys</title>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <script src="htmx.min.js"></script>
    <style href="bulma.min.css" />
    <style>
      :root {
        --base: #cfcfcf;
        --text: #212121;
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --base: #212121;
          --text: #cfcfcf;
        }
      }

      html {
        color-scheme: dark light;
      }

      :root:has(#theme [value="light"]:checked) {
        color-scheme: light;
        --base: #cfcfcf;
        --text: #212121;
      }

      :root:has(#theme [value="dark"]:checked) {
        color-scheme: dark;
        --base: #212121;
        --text: #cfcfcf;
      }

      body {
        color: var(--text);
        background-color: var(--base);
      }

      body {
        font-family: system-ui;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    
  <h1 class="title">My Paper Keys</h1>
  <p>Paper keys are the best account recovery mechanism. Create a key. Print the key and store it in a safe place. If you lose access to your account in the future, you can sign in using any paper key.</p><h2>50dfde58-6955-7e4e-c38d-59ee96f4fdbe</h2><h2>6c61681e-6ae1-8c71-180d-e4913bf7f419</h2><h2 class="title">Create New Paper Key</h2>
  <form method="post" action="" class="form">
    &lt; class="field">
      <label for="name" class="label">Name:</label>
      <input name="name" class="input" value="" />
      <input type="submit" name="Create" class="button" />
    </div>
  </form>

  </body>
</html>